---
title: 08 - AI Summarization Sequence Diagram
---
sequenceDiagram
 autonumber
 participant UI as Browser UI
 participant API as FastAPI
 participant Store as JobStore
 participant W as JobWorker
 participant S as Summarizer
 participant C as Summary disk cache
 participant L as Configured LLM endpoint
 UI->>API: POST /api/jobs/{id}/summary {template}
 API->>Store: Require result and status complete or failed
 API->>API: Require llm.enabled
 API->>Store: Set kind=summary, status=queued, template
 API-->>UI: HTTP 202 {job_id}
 W->>Store: Pick job / set running / result(job_id)
 Store-->>W: Edited turns and revision snapshot
 W->>W: Clear flagged on reviewed turns / stage M6
 W->>S: summarize(turns)
 S->>S: Split text to bounded chunks, preserving turn IDs
 loop Each chunk
  S->>C: Read identity + text + source-ID cache key
  alt Valid cache hit
   C-->>S: Validated summary JSON
  else Cache miss or invalid entry
   loop Up to 2 JSON / ID attempts
    S->>L: Completion request (chunk text and allowed IDs)
    L-->>S: Completion text
    S->>S: validate_summary(require_grounded=True)
   end
   S->>C: Save validated chunk response
  end
 end
 S->>S: Merge unique items / propagate uncertainty from flags
 S-->>W: Summary fields
 W->>Store: Save summary_json and snapshot summary_revision
 W->>Store: Set status=complete
 UI->>API: GET /api/jobs/{id}/result
 API->>Store: result() / derive stale and resolve evidence
 Store-->>API: Sources use transcript timestamps and speakers
 API-->>UI: Edited minutes and summary_stale
 Note over W,Store: If regeneration raises an exception, job becomes failed.<br/>POST /retry keeps kind=summary and reruns only M6.
 Note over S,L: Provider/network failures are not retried by the JSON repair loop.
